outputs.L1:
A circuit comprises an array of programmable memory elements fabricated upon a substrate, wherein each memory element possesses one or more processable regions that, when subjected to an external process in which a material is applied so as to at least partially cover one or more of said regions, are configured to program that memory element to one of multiple states;

a first set of control lines connected to the array of memory elements, whereby the contents of each individual memory element may be accessed by control signals applied to a respective combination of at least two control lines within the first set of control lines;

and an array of second circuit elements, distinct from the memory elements, each connected to a control line of the first set of control lines and to a further control line of a second set of control lines, distinct from the first set of control lines, thereby affording access to the second circuit elements within the array.
